1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:14,980
[upbeat music]

2
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:24,100
Look at me. I've never done this before. I want to try it, see what happens.

3
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:28,960
And also, you know, [clears throat] the game and the computer never get old.

4
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:34,820
Then I can see myself on the computer for a long time, you know, for, you know, just stay

5
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,960
at my age. I can get old, but the computer never gets old.

6
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,530
So I, I think I'd better keep my moves.

7
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:46,670
Maybe something I can move today, I may not be able to move in 10 years.

8
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:51,500
I have to keep my moves, keep my, keep my acting, keep my humor, put everything

9
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:55,339
into the computer. Then one day it's like, like a memory.

10
00:00:55,840 --> 00:01:00,780
It's a game, they show it to the audience, give it to the kids to play, and also they can

11
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,780
keep, keep, keep the memory for myself.

12
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:10,860
[upbeat music]

13
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,300
It's totally different from, from, from movies.

14
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:19,240
You know, uh, they make me do something, uh, like, uh, with nobody, just

15
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:24,900
acting alone. You have to pretend there's a, a helicopter.

16
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:27,160
You have to pretend the truck is coming, you go like this...

17
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:29,520
You know. Usually we do the real thing, you know.

18
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:32,700
The truck comes, boom, you get hit. You really get...

19
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,080
Now you really, you act for nothing.

20
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:39,160
You just act for the computer. But it's very interesting for me, yeah.

21
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:46,110
[upbeat music]

22
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:51,220
I play video games because the game really gives me a lot of ideas and, and keeps

23
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:54,800
my mind working. But now, games are harder.

24
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,900
Not like, uh, 10 years ago, 15 years ago.

25
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,480
It was simple, two buttons. But now, too many buttons.

26
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:01,680
You just, wow, it keeps you very busy.

27
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:08,540
[upbeat music]

28
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:11,340
They scan me every, every, like, uh, five hours.

29
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:17,720
So I, I think it's good. Why? Because after the scan, my face stays at this

30
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:20,300
age, never changes. I hope so.

31
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:29,880
[upbeat music]

32
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:34,800
I want to put in more humor. It's not, uh, just the fighting.

33
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,420
Humor and comedy, that's the most important.

34
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:44,560
I don't like violence. But between violence and action there's a big dilemma.

35
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,180
Everybody thinks action is violence, but look at my movies.

36
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:52,520
I like action, so I put in as little violence as possible.

37
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:57,520
Even in the game, I tell them to put in more comedy, show my physical jumps,

38
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:03,420
kicks. Hmm, then kids can learn from all the moves, jumping, spinning, kicking,

39
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:06,780
you know, punching. It's like, uh, exercise.

40
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:12,960
[upbeat music]

41
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:18,200
Nowadays American movies have lots and lots of explosions, lots of shootouts.

42
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:23,960
So I tell myself: "No explosions, no guns." I want something totally different from the

43
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,280
other action stars. So when they have, like, blood coming out of the nose,

44
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:33,360
out of the mouth, okay, in my movie there's no blood. Even with bam, bam, bam, bam, bam,

45
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,680
people get up, no bruises, nothing. It's...

46
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:42,440
I, I, I want to be like a comic book. That's why I fight with the ladder, and, uh,

47
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:47,160
with the stick, with everything. But when I come to America, a lot of directors ask me:

48
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:50,540
"How can you do that? How can you fight with the ladder?

49
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:52,700
How can you jump over the, the, the building?

50
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:56,340
How do you do all the, uh, uh, choreography, all the fight scenes?"

51
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:01,120
These things are easy for me. So I think it's a different kind of world, yeah.

52
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:07,420
[upbeat music]

53
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:23,340
Me?

54
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:25,460
Jackie.

55
00:04:27,219 --> 00:04:41,479
[upbeat music]

56
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:44,000
